---
import DocumentLayout from '../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import { pages } from '../data/pages';
---

<DocumentLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="A clear picture of local processing, ordinary website requests, and your choices."
  eyebrow="UPDATED OCTOBER 27, 2026"
  metaTitle={pages.privacy.metaTitle}
  metaDescription={pages.privacy.metaDescription}
>
  <h2>Your images stay local</h2>
  <p>
    Core image decoding, resizing, compression, conversion, cropping, metadata
    inspection, and ZIP creation happen in your browser. The application does
    not send selected image bytes, filenames, EXIF/GPS information, or generated
    output to an application server or conversion API. These values are not
    attached to analytics, placed in page URLs, or logged in production.
  </p>
  <p>
    File selection and drag-and-drop read files into the current tab. Local
    previews use temporary browser object URLs. Copy controls write explicitly
    selected metadata to your clipboard, and downloads create files on your
    device. Clearing the workspace releases application references and preview
    URLs; browser internals, extensions, clipboard history, and downloaded files
    operate outside that boundary.
  </p>
  <h2>Ordinary website requests</h2>
  <p>
    Visiting a website makes requests for HTML, scripts, styles, fonts, and
    sample artwork. The optional “Try a sample” control fetches an image bundled
    with this site, not an image from your device. Hosting providers may process
    connection details such as IP address, requested path, headers, and access
    timestamps for delivery, security, and operations.
  </p>
  <h2>Local preferences</h2>
  <p>
    The selected light/dark theme is stored in this browser’s local storage
    under a site preference key. Images, EXIF values, and output are not saved
    in a persistent application history. You can remove the preference through
    browser site-data settings. Your browser may separately retain form or
    download history.
  </p>
  <h2>Metadata and location</h2>
  <p>
    Metadata inspection is local. GPS fields are revealed only on request and
    are never turned into map links or shareable URLs. Select metadata
    deliberately before copying or saving it. Re-encoding an image without its
    original EXIF/GPS blocks does not guarantee anonymity: visible image
    content, filenames, and encoder-generated information may still be
    identifying.
  </p>
  <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    The default site has analytics and advertising disabled. It makes no
    requests to tracking or ad providers. If the operator later enables optional
    services, this policy must identify the actual providers, data, purposes,
    retention, and choices. Third-party scripts may receive ordinary browsing
    information even though core image operations remain local.
  </p>
  <p>
    Applicable consent requirements must be addressed before enabling ads. A
    generic cookie banner does not by itself establish compliance. Selected
    images, filenames, clipboard data, output, and metadata must never be
    included in analytics events or ad requests.
  </p>
  <h2>Links and contact</h2>
  <p>
    External documentation links are governed by their destinations’ policies.
    The local feedback form does not submit a message to this site. With a
    configured contact address it opens a draft in your email application;
    otherwise it saves a text draft on your device.
  </p>
  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    Use a trusted device and browser, prefer non-sensitive examples, clear the
    workspace after use, and manage downloaded output and clipboard history. See
    the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> for privacy questions. Operator
    details and jurisdiction-specific rights should be reviewed before public
    launch.
  </p>
</DocumentLayout>
